 105 00413 0000 VCTEXT, .-.     / Display text on screen, using inline params
 106                            / Inline param1: Address of text string
 107                            / Return follows with AC = 0
 108                            / Text is packed 6-bit stripped ASCII,
 109                            / where @ marks end of string and % is CRLF.
 110                            / Uses: VCvariables
 111 00414 7200         CLA
 112 00415 1613         TAD I   VCTEXT  / get text pointer
 113 00416 3236         DCA     VCTXPT
 114 00417 2213         ISZ     VCTEXT  / bump
 115            VCTLP,
 116 00420 1636         TAD I   VCTXPT  / get a pair of characters
 117 00421 7002         BSW
 118 00422 0235         AND     C077    / extract first
 119 00423 7450         SNA             / test for end of string
 120 00424 5613         JMP I   VCTEXT  /   if so, return
 121 00425 4237         JMS     VCCHAR  / else display it
 122 00426 1636         TAD I   VCTXPT
 123 00427 0235         AND     C077    / extract second
 124 00430 7450         SNA             / test for end of string
 125 00431 5613         JMP I   VCTEXT  /   if so, return
 126 00432 4237         JMS     VCCHAR  / else display it
 127 00433 2236         ISZ     VCTXPT
 128 00434 5220         JMP     VCTLP
 129            
 130 00435 0077 C077,   0077    / mask to extract a byte
 131 00436 0000 VCTXPT, .-.     / pointer to char string
 132            
 133 00437 0000 VCCHAR, .-.     / Display char from AC on screen
 134                            / Char is in 6 bit trimmed ASCII
 135                            / returns AC=0
 136 00440 1273         TAD     NPCSGN  / compare with EOL
 137 00441 7450         SNA
 138 00442 5262         JMP     VCCHCR  / got a %, use as CRLF
 139 00443 1274         TAD     PPCSGN  / undo the damage
 140 00444 7104         CLL RAL         / 2 words per char
 141 00445 1270         TAD     VCTTAP  / make address of table entry
 142 00446 3275         DCA     VCCHPT  / save pointer to char
 143 00447 1675         TAD I   VCCHPT  / get first 2 columns
 144 00450 4276         JMS     VCDCOL  / display first column
 145 00451 4276         JMS     VCDCOL  / display second column
 146 00452 2275         ISZ     VCCHPT
 147 00453 1675         TAD I   VCCHPT  / get second 2 columns
 148 00454 4276         JMS     VCDCOL  / display third column
 149 00455 4276         JMS     VCDCOL  / display final column
 150 00456 1345         TAD     VCXTMP
 151 00457 1271         TAD     VCDOTS
 152 00460 3345         DCA     VCXTMP  / advance over interchar column
 153 00461 5637         JMP I   VCCHAR
